<description>
Repeat each 3x3 control-center sprite toward the matching solid rectangle until a copy first overlaps that rectangle.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color.
- Each sprite is a 3x3 foreground object whose eight border pixels have one color and whose center has a different control color.
- For every control color, there is exactly one separate solid rectangular object of that color.

Rule
- Match each sprite to the unique solid rectangle whose color equals the sprite center.
- Copy the whole 3x3 sprite in the cardinal direction of that rectangle, stepping by three cells each time.
- Stop after pasting the first copy whose 3x3 bbox overlaps the rectangle; copied pixels overwrite the rectangle there.

Key insight
The center pixel is not the paint color: it is a destination key, while the entire 3x3 sprite is the motif tiled along the straight path.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "3x3 sprite s with a uniform border color and a different control-color center",
  "path": "straight cardinal path from s toward d",
  "trajectory": "copy s every three cells until the first copied bbox overlaps d",
  "dst": "separate solid rectangle d whose color matches s.center",
  "transform": "copied sprites overwrite background/rectangle cells; all other input pixels remain unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 20-25 rows x 20-25 cols, background 8
  sprites:
    count: 2-5 per grid
    shape: 3x3 solid; 8 border cells share one body color, center cell has a different control color
    body_color: single color shared by all sprites, distinct from all target colors
    center_color: matches exactly one target rectangle's color (multiple sprites may share a target)
  rectangles:
    count: 2-4 distinct solid monochromatic rectangles
    color: each rectangle color equals the center color of 1+ sprites
    dimensions: each side 2-18; both sides > 1
  alignment:
    each sprite has exactly one cardinal direction to its matched rectangle (row-overlap XOR col-overlap)
    gap (bg cells between sprite edge and rect near-edge) satisfies gap % 3 == 1; range 1-10
    copies tiled = gap // 3 + 1; range 1-4
  path:
    3-cell-wide corridor between sprite and target is all background
    all copy positions stay within grid bounds
    copies from different sprites do not overlap each other [observed]
  output:
    tile the full 3x3 sprite every 3 cells toward target; stop at first copy overlapping the rectangle
    copied sprite pixels overwrite background and rectangle cells; everything else unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (place rectangles and compute sprite positions from gap constraint)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size 20-25. Choose 2-4 target colors + 1 body color (all distinct, none = 8).
    2. Place 2-4 solid rectangles (sides 2-18) on the grid with generous spacing.
    3. For each rectangle, assign 1-2 sprites targeting it (total 2-5 sprites).
    4. For each sprite, pick a cardinal direction and a gap with gap % 3 == 1 (1-10).
       Compute sprite position = rect edge - (gap + 3) along that axis, aligned within rect perp span.
    5. Verify the 3-wide corridor from sprite to rect is clear of all other objects and in bounds.
       On failure, retry sprite placement or reduce gap.
    6. Place each sprite (body border + center color) on the grid. Input is complete.
```
